{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0CL4", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-proper}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:68ceb72f96e35984308912d7816dbd3156528b96344218667458810b44aeeb2b", "source_text": "Proper morphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d19cc9591ee6ed3ebbad959c8358a86e01df1fa59b906de236f42e5ffddbc338", "unit_id": "tag:0CL4:title"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0CL4", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dad1edb3c1113c0931b36001d2dc688b992eb62b54901bd80f2a49791ac5ea95", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe notion of a proper morphism plays an important role in algebraic geometry.\nHere is the definition of a proper morphism of algebraic stacks.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d496159ff0e2462f9ea318c07f36830929899e675100a6f1c1b9542403c50f61", "unit_id": "tag:0CL4:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0CL4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-proper}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1f93466531620815f3586eb4b46eeecc64693912818730b6d19ce234e52d2b29", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1d712e79f4500b649b31b2b713c733c7b54169e19695854993f3045f09fea1a1", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>\nbe a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nWe say <MATH_0002> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>proper<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if <MATH_0003> is separated, finite type, and\nuniversally closed.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:72f709f4f236a15dcc0f109728322177b90b6c6bff351da10e26531ae87bcdd4", "unit_id": "tag:0CL5:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0CL4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-definition-proper}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-representable-separated-diagonal-closed}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{section-finite-type}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-characterize-representable-universally-closed}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{stacks-properties-section-properties-morphisms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1f93466531620815f3586eb4b46eeecc64693912818730b6d19ce234e52d2b29", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cb68a8103abfb8e503a327ed7891a0ea1dd183807df56d8440e0932b18a1b450", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis does not conflict with the already existing notion of a proper morphism\nof algebraic spaces: a morphism of algebraic spaces is proper if and only if\nit is separated, finite type, and universally closed\n(Morphisms of Spaces, Definition <REF_0001>)\nand we've already checked the compatibility of these notions in\nLemma <REF_0002>,\nSection <REF_0003>, and\nLemmas <REF_0004>.\nSimilarly, if <MATH_0001> is a\nmorphism of algebraic stacks which is representable by algebraic spaces\nthen we have defined what it means for <MATH_0002> to be proper in\nProperties of Stacks, Section\n<REF_0005>.\nHowever, the discussion in that section shows that this is\nequivalent to requiring <MATH_0003> to be separated, finite type, and\nuniversally closed and the same references as above give the\ncompatibility.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:aaa50f5617f3bec3fcddfc7bb3aa21cf7b27571e72ad4b741a85c551895bc8db", "unit_id": "tag:0CL4:prose-0002"}
